    _intro_md = "# The inverse Turing test\n\nHumans are famously bad at *being random*. A normal Turing test asks\nwhether a machine can pass for a human; this one flips it around — can\n**you** produce a coin-flip sequence a machine couldn't tell apart from\nits own?\n\nFlip coins with the floating pad: click **0** / **1**, or click once and\nthen just tap the `0` and `1` keys. Every chart below re-computes live\nand compares your sequence to what *pure randomness* would look like.\n\nBased on the [calmcode blog post](https://calmcode.io/blog/inverse-turing-test).\nTry to get to ~50–100 flips."
